<title>CANADA: Saskatchewan Wheat Pool averts strike.</title>
<headline>Saskatchewan Wheat Pool averts strike.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saskatchewan Wheat Pool, Canada's largest grain handler, said on Friday it averted a strike by its 400 unionized workers.</p>
<p>Vice President Don Slobodzian said that 55 percent of unionized workers voted to strike, which fell short of the 75 percent threshold for a strike required by the Grain Services Union.</p>
<p>Talks broke down after the office workers' two-year contract expired on January 31.</p>
<p>SWP and the GSU have scheduled a meeting with a federal mediator for next Thursday.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
